# Third-party components

## jrt-fs.jar — OpenJDK

`public/java-playground/jrt-fs.jar` is taken unmodified from an OpenJDK 17
distribution (Eclipse Temurin). It is the reader that lets a compiler open a JDK
module image (`lib/modules`).

It is needed because CheerpJ's Java 17 runtime ships the module image but not this
reader, and its `/lt` mount is read-only — so the playground assembles a usable JDK
in its own writable directory at run time. See
`src/lib/java-playground/constants.ts` for the mechanics.

OpenJDK is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version 2, with the
Classpath Exception**. The Classpath Exception permits linking with this file
without extending the GPL to the linking work.

- License: https://openjdk.org/legal/gplv2+ce.html
- Source: https://github.com/openjdk/jdk17u

## Eclipse Compiler for Java (ECJ)

`public/java-playground/ecj-*.jar` is downloaded from Maven Central at build time
by `scripts/fetch-java-playground-assets.mjs` and is **not** stored in this
repository. It is served to the browser as a static asset, unmodified.

ECJ is licensed under the **Eclipse Public License 2.0**.

- License: https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/
- Source: https://github.com/eclipse-jdt/eclipse.jdt.core

