## Simulation libraries cited by the curriculum

Neither of these is redistributed in this repository. The lessons in
`src/content/frc/frc-sim-tools/` quote their public APIs and describe how to adopt them,
and each page cites the files it was written against.

- **FuelSim** (https://github.com/hammerheads5000/FuelSim), FRC 5000 Hammerheads' fuel
  physics simulation, is licensed **MIT**. It is distributed as a single source file that
  a team copies into its own robot project; a copy has to keep the licence header naming
  the copyright holder.
- **maple-sim** (https://github.com/Shenzhen-Robotics-Alliance/maple-sim) from the
  Shenzhen Robotics Alliance is licensed **BSD 3-Clause**. It ships as a vendordep and
  depends on the dyn4j rigid-body engine (https://dyn4j.org/).

## Authorship by section

Tools, Java, Practice and Kit Bot were written by FRC 4451 for this site and carry no
third-party licence. Java and Practice take direct inspiration from the University of
South Carolina's CSCE 145, CSCE 146, and MATH 374 (https://www.cse.sc.edu/~shephejj/csce145/,
.../csce146/, and https://thornef.github.io/math374/index.html). Kit Bot was written by the mentors from FRC 4864's build of *Scorpion*
(https://github.com/frc4451/Scorpion2026).
FRC combines Mantik's original lessons with FRC 4451's rewrites and additions; the PID
Tuning Practice group uses Mantik's practice project and tutorial videos. The base of the
Resources catalog is Mantik's work. Mantik's browser PID simulator was removed from this
fork in September 2026.

## Upstream repositories

GarageDocs is a fork of [itkan-robotics/mantik](https://github.com/itkan-robotics/mantik). The
site framework (Astro layout, navigation, search, content collections) is Mantik's work,
modified here; the curriculum text has been rewritten, and the FRC pages that keep a
Mantik outline cite it in their Sources block.
The Java playground under `src/lib/java-playground/`, `src/components/java-playground/`
and `scripts/java*` is ported from
[FRC3476/mantik-orange](https://github.com/FRC3476/mantik-orange), itself a fork of
that project.

**Neither upstream publishes a licence yet.** A licensing
request is open against itkan-robotics/mantik and has not yet been decided. Until
both licences are actually published, no licence can be granted for the parts of
this repository derived from them, so this fork carries no root `LICENSE` file. The
licences named above apply only to the third-party components and the FSC-derived
content they describe.

- Licensing request to itkan-robotics/mantik:
  https://github.com/itkan-robotics/mantik/issues/32

